  <h1>The sandboxes</h1>
  <p class="lead">Each section is a separate machine for making curves. Sampled drawings say so; the exact numbers carry their source.</p>



  <h2>0 · Mirrored Euler transforms</h2>
  <p class="lead">The same machine, with the chain broken in half. Each step is a p-triple
    turn, and the step after it is the <b>mirror</b> of that triple — its last two numbers
    swapped. For <code>(3,4,5)</code> the chain reads
    <code>(3,4,5)</code>, <code>(3,5,4)</code>, <code>(3,4,5)</code>, <code>(3,5,4)</code>.
    The first step keeps the circle; the mirror turns by a slightly different angle and
    grows, so the walk breathes instead of holding one radius. Every reading is a fraction
    of a turn; degrees are a readout, never an entry.</p>

