  <h2>0a · The lattice mobile</h2>
  <p class="lead">A spirograph whose every station is an integer point. Two arms each walk the
    integer points of their own circle, and the pen is their sum —
    <code>P = A[k·q] + B[k·p]</code> — so each station is the sum of two integer points and
    therefore an integer point itself. <b>Click a station to cut there</b>; the dashed stub is
    the branch, taken along the exact integer perpendicular of the incoming segment. The cost,
    said plainly: the integer points on a circle are not evenly spaced in angle, so the pen
    speeds up and slows down where they crowd, and the figures are coarser than a drawn
    spirograph. That is the price of every station being exact.</p>

