  <h2>0b · The prime mover</h2>
  <p class="lead">Instead of a straight parameter <code>t</code>, a pair of variables
    travels the circle. Each step is a <b>p-triple</b> divided by its hypotenuse — the triple
    <code>(3, 4, 5)</code> gives a turn of 53.13° and keeps the length at exactly 1 — so a walk
    of them stays on the <b>integer circle</b> and every position is a ratio of whole numbers.
    A complex step is refused: a step like <code>2 + i</code> has a length that is not a ratio,
    and that length would ride along in every position afterwards. Orange is the positive walk, blue the
    negative (the conjugate: different points, not the same ones backwards). PM2 is the
    same walk retarded by a lag; <b>brown</b> is the two added station by station, drawn
    with a Catmull-Rom spline so the curve between the lattice points is visible.</p>
